# ============================================================
# Project data / generated artifacts
# (large or regeneratable from the scripts next to them — not source code)
# Audited before the first real push to GitHub against its actual limits:
#   - hard block: any single file over 100MB (a normal `git push` rejects it outright)
#   - soft guidance: keep total repo size well under ~1GB for a healthy clone
# Everything NOT listed below IS tracked normally: all source code, all small CSVs
# (IAM/doctor splits, results, labels, cleaning/leakage reports), small config/
# tokenizer/checkpoint-metadata files, and CRNN's own checkpoints (~21MB each, under
# the limit, tracked on purpose).
# NOTE: the project used to live one level down, under final_code/ - that folder was
# flattened away (everything moved up into the repo root) on 2026-08-24, so every
# pattern below is now relative to the repo root directly, not final_code/. previous_code/
# and log_file/ were moved OUT of the repo entirely at the same time (now siblings of
# this repo folder), so neither needs an entry here anymore.
# ============================================================

# --- Files over GitHub's 100MB hard limit — a normal `git push` will reject these.
#     Needs a separate transfer (Git LFS, cloud storage, manual copy, etc.).
#     Every TrOCR model.safetensors is ~1.3GB, wherever it lives - caught unconditionally
#     below rather than listed path-by-path, so a newly-finished pipeline's checkpoint
#     (or a resumed numbered checkpoint-N/ that briefly reappears) is never missed.
#     Currently on disk (~1.3GB each): checkpoint/normal/trocr/model.safetensors;
#     checkpoint/doctor/trocr/{baseline,clhaa}/final/model.safetensors;
#     checkpoint/doctor/trocr_pilot/{baseline,clhaa,fajardo,benitez}/final/model.safetensors ---
**/model.safetensors
**/optimizer.pt

# --- Raw/derived image folders. No single file here is anywhere near 100MB, but each
#     is thousands of individual files (2k-34k) - committing that many blows past the
#     soft repo-size guidance and makes clones slow. All regenerable from the scripts
#     documented in RUN_ORDER.md, given the right upstream data. Sizes: I_Am_Dataset/
#     ~1.6GB/34k+ files; doctor_raw/images/ ~58MB/10,347 files; doctor_clean/images/
#     ~57MB/10,050 files; preprocessed_doctor/ ~160MB/32,160 files;
#     preprocessed_doctor_test/ ~25MB/4,020 files (baseline+clhaa - both models' winners) ---
data/normal/I_Am_Dataset/
data/doctor/doctor_raw/images/
data/doctor/doctor_clean/images/
data/doctor/preprocessed_doctor/
data/doctor/preprocessed_doctor_test/

# --- combineDataset.py's 3 raw source folders, extracted directly into doctor_raw/
# (see combineDataset.py's SOURCE_FOLDERS) - not this project's own output, just the
# original downloads sitting alongside it, never meant to be committed. "89" is the
# extracted "Doctor Handwriting Recognition Dataset" zip - named "89" (not the zip's own
# name) to match the `source` value already baked into the live labels.csv - see
# combineDataset.py's SOURCE_FOLDERS comment for why. ---
data/doctor/doctor_raw/89/
data/doctor/doctor_raw/RxHand Original/
data/doctor/doctor_raw/Doctor’s Handwritten Prescription BD dataset/

# --- the 3 raw zips themselves, if placed directly in doctor_raw/ for
# ensure_source_folders_extracted() to auto-unzip - also never meant to be committed ---
data/doctor/doctor_raw/*.zip

# --- Internal working notes, not part of the handed-in submission (RUN_ORDER.md is) ---
DATA_PROVENANCE.md
KNOWN_ISSUES.md